content:
C programming language was developed by Dennis Ritchie at Bell Labs in 1972. It is a general-purpose, procedural programming language.

Key Features of C:
- Simple and Efficient
- Portable
- Rich Library
- Modularity
- Middle-level language

Basic Structure of C Program:

#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    printf("Hello World");
    return 0;
}

C is widely used in system programming, embedded systems, and developing operating systems like UNIX.

Data Types in C:
- int: Integer values
- float: Decimal numbers
- char: Single character
- double: Large decimal numbers

Variables are containers for storing data values. In C, you must declare the type of variable before using it.

Example:
int age = 20;
float price = 99.99;
char grade = 'A';

Variables are memory locations used to store data. Each variable in C has a specific type.

Rules for naming variables:
1. Must start with letter or underscore
2. Can contain letters, digits, underscores
3. Case-sensitive
4. Cannot use keywords

Data Types:

Primary Data Types:
- int (2 or 4 bytes)
- float (4 bytes)
- char (1 byte)
- double (8 bytes)

Derived Data Types:
- Arrays
- Pointers
- Structures
- Unions

Example Program:
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int a = 10;
    float b = 5.5;
    char c = 'X';
    printf("Integer: %d\n", a);
    printf("Float: %.2f\n", b);
    printf("Character: %c\n", c);
    return 0;
}

Control structures determine the flow of program execution.

If Statement:
if (condition) {
    // code
}

If-Else:
if (condition) {
    // true block
} else {
    // false block
}

Else-If Ladder:
if (marks >= 90) grade = 'A';
else if (marks >= 70) grade = 'B';
else grade = 'C';

Switch Case:
switch(expression) {
    case 1: printf("One"); break;
    case 2: printf("Two"); break;
    default: printf("Other");
}

Loops:
- for loop
- while loop
- do-while loop
